189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 156 0 R
/E (A huge part of this progress depends on working with biological data. In such a field it is not uncommon to analyse DNA and protein sequences, perhaps to predict how tumours evolve, or model antibody structures to understand how they bind their targets, maybe map how immune cells interact with cancer, and design new proteins that behave in specific ways inside the body. We hope to show you just some of the technologies/techniques powering immunotherapy outcomes.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
