229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 160 0 R
/T (In contrast to more traditional vaccines, which serve as preventative action against infectious diseases, personalised mRNA cancer vaccines are designed to elicit an immune response against cancer already present in the body. )
/E (In contrast to more traditional vaccines, which serve as preventative action against infectious diseases, personalised mRNA cancer vaccines are designed to elicit an immune response against cancer already present in the body. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 160 0 R
/T (The main targets of these vaccines are neoantigens, abnormal proteins resulting from mutations in the cancerous tumour cells. Because neoantigens are absent from healthy tissues, the immune system can readily recognise them as foreign and mount targeted responses to cells which express them. This separates neoantigens from other tumour-associated antigens, which are also found in normal tissues and are frequently subject to immune tolerance. As a result, neoantigens are better-suited targets for mRNA vaccines, allowing a stronger, more specific immune response while minimising damage to healthy cells.)
/E (The main targets of these vaccines are neoantigens, abnormal proteins resulting from mutations in the cancerous tumour cells. Because neoantigens are absent from healthy tissues, the immune system can readily recognise them as foreign and mount targeted responses to cells which express them. This separates neoantigens from other tumour-associated antigens, which are also found in normal tissues and are frequently subject to immune tolerance. As a result, neoantigens are better-suited targets for mRNA vaccines, allowing a stronger, more specific immune response while minimising damage to healthy cells.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 160 0 R
/T (Constructing a personalised vaccine begins with sequencing DNA and RNA from a patient's tumour and creating a profile of mutations unique to that individual's cancer.)
/E (Constructing a personalised vaccine begins with sequencing DNA and RNA from a patient's tumour and creating a profile of mutations unique to that individual's cancer.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
