/P 163 0 R
/T (Immune checkpoints are the result of interactions between cell receptors and ligands. Two of the best-characterised checkpoint pathways are programmed cell death protein 1 \(PD-1\) and cytotoxic T-lymphocyte-associated protein 4 \(CTLA-4\).)
/E (Immune checkpoints are the result of interactions between cell receptors and ligands. Two of the best-characterised checkpoint pathways are programmed cell death protein 1 \(PD-1\) and cytotoxic T-lymphocyte-associated protein 4 \(CTLA-4\).)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
