/Title (Immune checkpoint inhibitors are monoclonal antibodies that inhibit the interaction between immune checkpoint molecules and T cells, allowing T cells to remain activated and attack cancer cells. In recent years, several drugs have been approved to target PD-1, PD-L1, and CTLA-4. Blocking PD-1 prevents inhibitory signalling within activated T-cells, whereas blocking PD-L1 prevents tumour cells from engaging PD-1, both acting to prolong the T-cell response. In contrast, inhibiting CTLA-4 restores CD28-mediated co-stimulatory signalling, promoting T-cell activation and expansion.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 786 0 R
/Next 768 0 R
>>
endobj
